Subject: client: feed raw window sizes and every frame to the resize module

Wires the settle and the stall detector from the previous patch into the
client.

- message.c: lgMessage_process hands each posted window size, with the
  time core_updatePositionInfo posted it, to core_onWindowSizeRaw before
  the debounce, so the settle counts from the raw change.
- core.c: core_onWindowSizeRaw calls resize_raw. core_resizeFrameSeen
  counts each frame in an atomic, and core_resizeUpdate calls
  resize_seen on the main thread when the count moves. A new session
  starts from the current count.
- main.c: main_frameThread calls core_resizeFrameSeen for each frame,
  beside the frame counter.
- config_message_test.c: the cases that checked the debounce through the
  ask now check its "window is" log line, cases that wait for an ask
  wait for the settle or the gap, and new cases cover the raw feed
  (size A, then size B 1.8 s later, asks only for B, 2 s after B) and
  the frame count.
- tests/CMakeLists.txt: registers the new resize and config-message
  cases.

No message is added and no message's format changes.

